      "n_contexts": 1,
      "answer": "Southwest's 737 MAX 8 fleet (87 aircraft as of January 1, 2024) is compliant with FAA AD 2020-05-11 (pre-service compliance Nov 2020) and FAA AD 2022-03-07 (completed April 2022). For FAA AD 2024-01-02 (MCAS Software v2.0 installation), compliance is due - deadline May 15, 2024 - with all 87 aircraft currently on MCAS v1.7.3 and software updates scheduled February-May 2024 (phased, ~10 aircraft/month). The target is MCAS v2.0 per Boeing SB Rev 2. Separately, a non-Southwest record (G-ABCD) flags anticipated non-compliance with the same AD, noting the deadline has not yet been reached and the aircraft remains airworthy under MCAS v1.7.3 until then.",
